age loans. In addition, the company offers annuity and life insurance products, such as deferred and immediate annuities, as well as indexed universal life insurance products; and funding agreements and pension risk transfer (PRT) solutions. Further, it engages in the real estate brokerage business. Fidelity National Financial, Inc. was incorporated in 2005 and is headquartered in Jacksonville, Florida.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Michael Joseph Nolan | Chief Executive Officer | Age 65 | Compensation: $5.7M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 24K people. Revenue per employee of $589K ranks in the above the sector median among Financial Services peers, with revenue growing 6%/yr across its filed history. Stock-based compensation of $4K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 10\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (4/10).","financial_summary":["Fidelity National Financial, In is a large-cap financial services business with a $11.7B market cap on $14.4B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +8% over the past three years and +5% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 17% against a 8% cost of capital, a 9-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.7\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage runs at 7.1\u00d7.","Management returns a meaningful 5.8% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 5.8% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.4\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.3) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Operating margins 18% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Price sits 27% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.271206961517182},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 5.2% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Significant insider selling (net $7.2M)","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","dollars":-7153734.58},{"text":"High market volatility with VIX at 36, signaling elevated fear","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Widening credit spreads suggest growing stress in corporate debt markets","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Valued at a 55% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","20 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Technical Reactions to FNF Trends in Macro Strategies","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/134/Technical_Reactions_to_FNF_Trends_in_Macro_Strategies_111926024802_1795074482.html","date":"2026-11-19","timestamp":1795074482.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Critical Review: Neptune Insurance (NYSE:NP) and Fidelity National Financial (NYSE:FNF)","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/16/critical-review-neptune-insurance-nysen